# AN INSTRUMENT, NEVER THE PRODUCT: THE GHOST VARIANT'S GATE AS A PICTURE (2026-10-11). On top of v-ghost: every pixel
# that takes the variant's own path (the mask says an occluder was found) comes out as one flat colour, 4 0 4, which no
# picture of the game holds. A replay through this library is the map of where v-ghost may change the picture; held
# against the difference of v-ghost's picture from the product's it says whether anything changed outside the gate.
what AN INSTRUMENT (the picture changes): with v-ghost, every pixel of the variant's own path is painted one flat colour (4 0 4): the gate's map
passes ffx_frameinterpolation_pass
wave64 the same edit in both variants: the pass has no wave operation
file framegeneration/fsr3/include/gpu/frameinterpolation/ffx_frameinterpolation.h
--- old
        fInterpolatedColor = ffxLerp(ofColor, fInterpolatedColor, ffxSaturate(fGameMvBias));
--- new
        fInterpolatedColor = ffxLerp(ofColor, fInterpolatedColor, ffxSaturate(fGameMvBias));
        // (the instrument v-ghost-show-gate)
        if (bGhost)
        {
            fInterpolatedColor = FfxFloat32x3(4.0f, 0.0f, 4.0f);
            fInPaintingWeight  = 0.0f;      // and the inpainting pass leaves the paint alone
        }
--- end
